%% Diagrama 2: Sequência de Transferência PIX
%% Fluxo completo desde autenticação até publicação de evento

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    
    %% Participants
    actor Client as 👤 Client
    participant API as 🚀 BankingCore.API<br/>(ASP.NET Core)
    participant Auth as 🔐 JWT Middleware<br/>(RS256 Verification)
    participant Validator as ✅ Validator<br/>(FluentValidation)
    participant UseCase as 🎯 UseCase<br/>(TransferPixUseCase)
    participant DB as 🗄️ MySQL 8.0<br/>(Stored Procedures)
    participant EventPub as 📢 EventPublisher<br/>(Kafka Producer)
    participant Consumer as 🔄 Consumer<br/>(Async Workers)
    
    %% Request flow
    Client->>+API: POST /api/pix/transfer<br/>Authorization: Bearer {JWT}<br/>X-Idempotency-Key: {GUID}
    
    %% JWT validation
    API->>+Auth: Validate JWT Token
    Auth->>Auth: Verify RS256 signature<br/>Extract user_id from claims
    Auth-->>-API: ✅ Authenticated<br/>user_id: {GUID}
    
    %% Input validation
    API->>+Validator: Validate TransferRequest
    Validator->>Validator: Check amount > 0<br/>Validate account IDs<br/>Verify idempotency key format
    Validator-->>-API: ✅ Valid request
    
    %% Business logic
    API->>+UseCase: Execute transfer
    Note over UseCase,DB: Clean Architecture:<br/>Application orchestrates,<br/>Infrastructure executes
    
    UseCase->>+DB: CALL sp_process_pix_transfer(
    Note right of DB: START TRANSACTION<br/>🔒 FOR UPDATE NOWAIT
    
    DB->>DB: 1️⃣ Check idempotency<br/>(idempotency_key EXISTS?)
    DB->>DB: 2️⃣ Lock source account<br/>(SELECT FOR UPDATE)
    DB->>DB: 3️⃣ Validate balance<br/>(≥ transfer amount)
    DB->>DB: 4️⃣ Debit source account<br/>(UPDATE accounts)
    DB->>DB: 5️⃣ Credit target account<br/>(UPDATE accounts)
    DB->>DB: 6️⃣ Insert DEBIT transaction
    DB->>DB: 7️⃣ Insert CREDIT transaction<br/>(with masked receiver name)
    
    Note right of DB: COMMIT TRANSACTION<br/>✅ Atomic operation
    
    DB-->>-UseCase: ✅ Transfer completed<br/>end_to_end_id: {E2E_ID}<br/>status: SETTLED
    
    %% Event publishing
    UseCase->>+EventPub: Publish PixTransferCompletedEvent
    Note right of EventPub: Event contains:<br/>• transaction_id<br/>• source_account_id<br/>• target_account_id<br/>• amount<br/>• end_to_end_id<br/>• timestamp
    
    EventPub->>EventPub: Serialize to JSON<br/>Publish to Kafka topic
    EventPub-->>-UseCase: ✅ Event published
    
    Note over EventPub,Consumer: Kafka guarantees:<br/>• At-least-once delivery<br/>• Ordered within partition<br/>• Consumer offset tracking
    
    UseCase-->>-API: ✅ TransferResponse
    API-->>-Client: 201 Created<br/>{transactionId, endToEndId, status}
    
    %% Async processing
    rect rgb(240, 248, 255)
        Note over Consumer: Background Processing<br/>(Eventually Consistent)
        EventPub-)Consumer: 📨 Consume event
        Consumer->>Consumer: Send notification<br/>Send email<br/>Update analytics<br/>Log audit trail
    end
    
    %% Error scenarios
    rect rgb(255, 240, 240)
        Note over API,DB: ❌ Error Scenarios
        Client-)API: Retry with same idempotency key
        API-)DB: CALL sp_process_pix_transfer
        DB-)DB: Detect duplicate<br/>Return original result
        DB--)API: ✅ Idempotent response<br/>(no duplicate debit)
        API--)Client: 200 OK<br/>(original transaction)
    end
